cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this replication package, please cite the paper below."
title: "Replication package: What Do Corporate Environmental Ratings Measure? Scale, Disclosure and Carbon Outcomes in European Listed Firms"
authors:
  - family-names: Chalak
    given-names: Sonia
  - family-names: Keshtkar
    given-names: Sadegh
  - family-names: Bidollahkhany
    given-names: Fereidoon
year: 2026
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sonia86119/environmental-capability-carbon-outcomes"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20814674"
abstract: >-
  Replication code for the study of whether an environmental rating tracks
  physical carbon outcomes among European listed firms, drawn from a raw
  universe of 4,329 instruments. Builds the analysis files from the LSEG
  extracts, estimates every model in the paper and draws every figure, and
  includes a variable dictionary, the data-access protocol and a synthetic
  demonstration dataset. The LSEG data are proprietary and are not included.
